file=Ops & Delivery/DEPARTMENT-WORKFLOW.md · s:=Cross-cutting operations dept. Process design (Deming) \· sprint cadence (per team) \· capacity (forward + gap) \· cross-team handoff discipline.\n · st:=**Leader: `flow`** (Deming persona). Others: `pace` \· `capacity` \· `handoff` — universal principles.\n · t:Tree=```\nTeams/Ops & Delivery/\n├── README.md \· DEPARTMENT-WORKFLOW.md\n├── flow/     (3 custom + Deming identity)\n├── pace/     (3 custom)\n├── capacity/ (3 custom)\n└── handoff/  (3 custom)\n```\n\n12 skills \· 0 marketplace.\n · rr:Routing rules=- flow routes multi-agent process questions.\n- Velocity is never comparative across teams (Deming — variation is intrinsic).\n- Capacity assumes sustainable pace; no overtime.\n- Every handoff has an envelope; no silent handoffs.\n · e:Escalation=L3 fixed to `Governance/board`. Always-L3:\n- flow: bottleneck external (supplier / market) \· SOP-owner systemic non-response\n- pace: systemic shift across all teams \· delivery >85% risk to critical date\n- capacity: gap > 3 FTE-months \· roadmap-blocking \· hire commitment > $5K/mo\n- handoff: silent-handoff pattern > 20% for a team \· critical-path blocking\n · tb=\| Case \| We do \| They do \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Strategy \| frame process implications \| `marcus` decides \| · tb=\| Fleet-level agent orchestration \| consume patterns \| `meta` owns \| · tb=\| Product roadmap priority \| consume \| `spec` + `vista` own \| · tb=\| Financial cost of decisions \| surface implications \| `felix` models \| · l:Logical=All 4 agents have Path-1 book-requirements.\n · f:Fleet=+4 (62 → 66). Routing rows added.\n